# AI Safety

## Allowed

- Local AI assistance (for example Python ML and Ollama) may be added in later phases for drafting, anomaly hints, or operator guidance suggestions.
- AI outputs are advisory only and require human review where they touch operational workflows.

## Prohibited

- AI must never make final food-safety decisions.
- AI must never make final QA verification decisions.
- AI must never authorize loading release.
- AI must never close CAPA.
- AI must never grant, deny, or escalate access control.
- No paid external AI API is required for core delivery.
- Core recording, review, and release workflows must not depend on AI availability.

## Controls

- Sensitive operational data sent to AI components must follow the AI safety policy.
- Prompt/output audit requirements apply where AI touches regulated workflows.
- Model versions used for assistance must be identifiable.
- On AI failure, fall back to deterministic human workflows without blocking recording.
